    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75">

                <pb facs="0179" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v5/pg149"/>

                <head>Mr. Bancroft to Mr.
                        Buchanan.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1848-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 19, 1848.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I send you a man of Vancouver’s Island,
                    recently published by James Wyld, geographer to the Queen. It purports to mark,
                    by a dotted line, the boundary between the United States and Great Britain. You
                    will see that this map suggests an encroachment on our rights by adopting a line
                    far to the east of the Straits of Haro. You may remember that Mr. Boyd, more
                    than two years ago, suggested to you that a design of preferring some such
                    claims existed. I inferred, from what I could learn at that time, that this
                    design grew up with the Hudson’s Bay Company, and I had no reason to suppose it
                    favored by the Colonial Secretary. * * *<seg type="margin">Mr. Bancroft
                        continues the suggestion that unjust claims may be made.</seg></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE BANCROFT.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Buchanan</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">D. C</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
